    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "```cython\r\ncdef bint contains_a_literal(unicode s) except? -1:\r\n    return \"a\" in s\r\n\r\ncdef bint contains_a_ucs4(unicode s) except? -1:\r\n    return <Py_UCS4>\"a\" in s\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe former turns into:\r\n\r\n```c\r\n  __pyx_t_1 = (__Pyx_PyUnicode_ContainsTF(__pyx_n_u_a, __pyx_v_s, Py_EQ)); if (unlikely(__pyx_t_1 < 0)) __PYX_ERR(0, 2, __pyx_L1_error)\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhereas the latter turns into:\r\n\r\n```c\r\n  __pyx_r = (__Pyx_UnicodeContainsUCS4(__pyx_v_s, ((Py_UCS4)97)));\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe latter allows the C compiler much more scope to optimize the code, as it turns into a simple loop rather than invoking `PyUnicode_Contains`.",
